<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lord William Campbell</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1730–<a href="/years/1778">1778</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lord William Campbell was a Scottish naval officer, governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nova-scotia">Nova Scotia</a> from 1766 to 1773 and the last royal governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-carolina">South Carolina</a>, arriving in Charleston in 1775. Unable to control the revolutionary authorities, he fled to a British warship in September 1775. He was wounded serving with the fleet in the attack on Sullivan's Island in 1776 and died in 1778.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lord-william-campbell.jpg" alt="Lord William Campbell" width="320" height="392" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Gainsborough · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lord_William_Campbell_(cropped)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
